      "translation_quote": "Hulle het ’n boupermit vir 10,000 akkers vir hul families en ander wat later kon kom ontvang."
    },
    {
      "location": "translation.html, paragraph 8",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "they made the trip across the Atlantic ... many German-dialect speakers",
      "suggested_fix": "Vervang “het hulle die Oseaan oorgemaak” met “het hulle die Atlantiese Oseaan oorgesteek” en “baie Duitssprekendes” met “baie sprekers van Duitse dialekte”.",
      "translation_quote": "het hulle die Oseaan oorgemaak ... baie Duitssprekendes"
    },
    {
      "location": "translation.html, first paragraph under Misverstand",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "Sometime, after being in Penn’s woods for a number of years ... built a substantial homestead",
      "suggested_fix": "Vervang “Irgendwannet” met “Op ’n stadium” en “’n aansienlike boerderij” met “’n aansienlike opstal”.",
      "translation_quote": "Irgendwannet, nadat hy ’n aantal jare in Penn se woude was ... ’n aansienlike boerderij"
    },
    {
      "location": "translation.html, second paragraph under Misverstand",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "riding to Philadelphia with furs then back out into the vast frontier with blankets, brass kettles",
      "suggested_fix": "Vervang die betrokke frase met “wat met pelse na Philadelphia gery het en dan met komberse, geelkoperketels en ander handelsware terug na die uitgestrekte grensgebied gereis het”. Dit herstel die foutiewe bewegingsfrase en die metaalsoort.",
      "translation_quote": "ry roerend na Philadelphia met velle en dan terug uit na die uitgestrekte grens met komberse, bronsketels"
    },
    {
      "location": "translation.html, paragraph under Medisyne",
      "severity": "minor",
      "source_quote": "live as a single sister ... being a blessing to the local community ... her homemade herbal medicines ... helped his father’s first wife minister to the many settlers",
